   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 3: Joining words"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "A **joining word** links two ideas. **And** adds, **but** shows a difference and **because** gives a reason.\n\nI like mangoes **and** apples. I like mangoes **but** not lemons. I wear a coat **because** it is cold."
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "emoji": "🥭➕🍎",
   "alt": "I like mangoes and apples. 'And' joins two things.",
   "caption": "I like mangoes and apples. 'And' joins two things."
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "prompt": "Fill in the joining word: I took an umbrella ___ it was raining.",
    "hint": "It gives a reason.",
    "options": [
     {
      "id": "a",
      "text": "but"
     },
     {
      "id": "b",
      "text": "and"
     },
     {
      "id": "c",
      "text": "because"
     }
    ],
    "answer": [
     "c"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "reveal",
   "prompt": "Can you finish this sentence? I am happy because ...",
   "answer_markdown": "Any reason works. For example: I am happy because it is Eid!"
  },
